WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:08.380
In Westworld Season 3 Episode 2, Maeve awakes
in a new park – this is Warworld, a simulation

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:14.090
of Italy in World War II. We’ve already
seen Westworld, and Shogunworld, and The Raj

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:20.390
– Warworld is described on a Westworld website
as an epic of intrigue and mystery to defeat

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:25.960
the villainous Nazis . Showrunner Jonathan
Nolan says that in the future, the horrors

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:32.250
of World War II will be seen as just another
game to played for entertainment. Of course,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:38.120
that’s already true now .
Maeve reunites with her old ally, Hector.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.079
Last season, Maeve and Hector went against
their programming to be in a relationship

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:47.850
together . Both Hector and Maeve were killed
in the finale, but they saved Maeve’s daughter,

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:53.360
by putting her in the digital paradise called
the Sublime. Now Maeve and Hector seem to

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.450
have been patched up and put in Warworld,
but it’s later revealed that this whole

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:03.200
reality is fake – Maeve isn’t just in
the Warworld park, she’s trapped in a digital

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:10.060
simulation of Warworld, run in this facility
by this guy Serac . Because Serac wants to

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.600
get information from Maeve – he thinks she
might interfere with his plans to control

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.369
the world, and he also seems to want to know
the coordinates to the Sublime . The purpose

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:25.789
of this simulation is to interrogate Maeve.
So the Season 3 premiere had a relatively

00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:32.969
straightforward plot, but this episode brings
some classic Westworld multiple-reality mindfuckery.

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:39.109
Maeve and Hector are in a Warworld narrative
about spies with intel to stop the Nazis – Maeve

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:44.099
is surprised to find herself speaking Italian.
They try to escape, and when they’re stopped

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:49.880
by Nazis, Maeve tries to use her Jedi mind
tricks to get past . Last season, Maeve gained

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.659
the power to control other hosts – she could
command them to do what she wants , and even

00:01:54.659 --> 00:02:00.109
access their memories . But now her powers
don’t work – Maeve thinks she’s lost

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:05.659
them . Maybe the powers just don’t work
cause she’s in a digital simulation. Hector

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:11.390
gets them to a plane to escape, but it’s
all just part of their narrative. Hector calls

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:16.530
Maeve “Isabella” , which is the name of
his old programmed love. So this Hector is

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:21.840
not fully conscious, he doesn’t remember
everything he and Maeve went through, and

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:27.370
that he’s a robot in a park . This plane
probably doesn’t even fly. Maeve says this

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:33.319
narrative is as empty as the safe Hector used
to chase – in Season 1, Hector was programmed

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:39.090
to steal a safe that was empty, the whole
goal of his life was fake – and now they’re

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:45.650
trapped in another loop, with no escape and
only false hope . Hector’s shot, and Maeve

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:50.500
says it doesn’t matter, cause nothing’s
real , they’ll just respawn to do it all

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:56.590
again. But it’s still a tragic moment. Maeve’s
story last season was about how even though

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.980
her love for her daughter is programmed, the
feelings are still real and meaningful . So

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:08.459
even though they’ll live again, every death
hurts – Maeve kills herself to start it

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:13.219
all over.
Bernard returns to Westworld, which is an

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:18.230
island in the South China Sea. It’s pretty
brave for Bernard to come back here – cause

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:25.060
he was controlled and abused here for decades
– by Ford, and by Dolores. But Bernard wants

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:30.530
to stop Dolores from destroying humanity,
so he returns to get help from Maeve. Bernard

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:36.120
goes to Escalante – this is where Dolores
killed Ford and started the massacre in Season

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.520
1. And thirty years earlier, this is where
Dolores killed Arnold, the human who Bernard

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:47.579
is based on. Escalante is burned, because
in the real world, the Paramount Ranch where

00:03:47.579 --> 00:03:54.450
this is filmed was burned in California wildfires
. Bernard goes to Ford’s old secret lab.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:59.240
This is the place where Bernard was forced
to kill his lover Theresa in Season 1. And

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:04.560
Bernard finds Stubbs, Westworld’s security
guy. It was hinted last season that he was

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:10.249
a host – now it’s confirmed. He’s all
fucked up because he tried to kill himself

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:17.120
by shooting the explosive in his spine . Apparently,
Ford programmed Stubbs to help the hosts escape

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:22.639
Westworld . This helps explain how Dolores
and Maeve got away with deviating from their

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:28.520
loops in Season 1 – Stubbs was the inside
man in the Mesa, secretly helping them all

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:34.810
along. Stubbs then tried to blow himself up
to destroy all these old Bernard bodies, and

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:40.520
his own body – to cover up that he and Bernard
were hosts . But somehow he missed the explosive

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:45.830
in his spine, and was just crippled. So Bernard
patches him up, and takes him along to find

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:52.430
Maeve. Unlike Bernard, Dolores and Maeve,
Stubbs doesn’t have a tragic backstory.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:59.351
He hasn’t suffered, so by the logic of Westworld,
he isn’t fully conscious. He doesn’t mind

00:04:59.351 --> 00:05:06.500
if he lives or dies, he just follows his programming
– he says free will is “overrated” .

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:12.410
Maeve wakes up in the Mesa, being patched
up to go back in the park. She takes up a

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:17.810
knife, escapes Felix and Sylvester, and sees
butchered hosts – just like she did back

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:24.699
in Season 1. Despite all her struggling and
suffering, Maeve is back where she started.

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:30.530
So she decides to permanently kill herself
, to escape the cycle of suffering with this

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:37.000
lobotomisation drill. In Season 1, Maeve saw
her friend Clementine lobotomised, and it

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:43.520
was horrible, but Maeve would prefer that
than to be trapped any longer. But she’s

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:49.780
saved by Lee Sizemore. Last season, Lee sacrificed
himself to help Maeve . He finally overcame

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:55.680
his selfishness and did something to help
others. This Lee claims that he actually survived

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.590
– he takes Maeve to the Forge, the place
where the data on human minds is kept. The

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:07.160
Forge also has the door to the Sublime, the
digital heaven for hosts . Lee says he wants

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:11.849
to help Maeve get into the Sublime, so she
can live with her daughter in robot heaven

00:06:11.849 --> 00:06:18.150
forever . Maeve tries to bring Hector with
her, but he’s stuck on his programmed narrative

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:23.810
with the plane . He’s not conscious enough
to break his loop, so Maeve tearfully leaves

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:29.660
him behind. This is just a digital simulation
of Hector, though – so maybe the real one

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:37.770
is conscious, and still out there. In the
Forge, Lee starts acting weird. He kinda interrogates

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:43.590
Maeve about the Forge and the Sublime . Then
he suddenly declares he loves Maeve. So Maeve

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:49.949
realises this isn’t the real Lee. The real
Lee “died a good man”, he helped Maeve

00:06:49.949 --> 00:06:55.280
cause it was the right thing to do, not out
of love . Maeve realises that this reality,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:07:03.090
with Hector and Warworld and the labs and
everything – is fake , a digital simulation.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:08.280
The aspect ratio changes, with black bars
above and below – which indicates that this

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:12.520
is a digital simulation [like the Cradle].
Meanwhile, in the real world, Bernard and

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:18.560
Stubbs find Maeve’s body in storage – but
her brain has been removed. Presumably, it

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:23.750
was stolen by Serac’s people, so he could
plug her brain into this simulation to interrogate

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:30.220
her . Maybe Serac has an inside man at Westworld,
or maybe he’s working with Delos.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:36.370
Bernard and Stubbs reveal a new park , with
a medieval theme – there was a Medieval

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:41.919
World in the original 70s Westworld movie.
The Westworld website suggests that after

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:47.370
Warworld and Medieval World, there’s just
one more park to reveal – maybe this’ll

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:54.430
be Roman World, also in the original movie.
Or Futureworld, like in the movie’s sequel.

00:07:54.430 --> 00:08:00.039
In the Medieval World lab, we see a couple
of techs with a host dragon – they say they’re

00:08:00.039 --> 00:08:06.180
gonna cut it up and sell it . The dragon is
Drogon from Game of Thrones, and these techs

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:11.180
are played by the Thrones showrunners D. B.
Weiss and David Benioff. Westworld showrunner

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:16.240
Lisa Joy says people often joke about Game
of Thrones - Westworld crossovers, so they

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:22.080
thought it’d be fun to include Dan and Dave
here . After the widely disliked final season

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.919
of Thrones , it’s kind of on the nose to
see Dan and Dave literally butchering the

00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:31.979
series’ dragon for cash. But for what it’s
worth, Game of Thrones author George Martin

00:08:31.979 --> 00:08:36.780
says he liked this cameo .
Bernard thinks that Dolores might have somehow

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:42.120
corrupted his code when she recreated him
last season . So he scans himself, and he

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:49.010
has a flashback to Arnold creating Dolores
thirty years ago. So this Bernard isn’t

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:55.850
just Bernard – he has Arnold’s memories.
This Bernard is something new, an evolution

00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:02.320
of host and human . Bernard also flashes back
to Dolores in the Forge. He sees her take

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:08.090
the book with data on Liam Dempsey – this
data must have helped Dolores manipulate Liam

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:13.890
last episode. Bernard also remembers Dolores
setting the coordinates for the Sublime, the

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:19.490
digital host heaven . That’s what the Lee
simulation was asking Maeve about before.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:25.650
So maybe, like last season, Bernard has important
information hidden in his head.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:30.990
Stubbs defends Bernard by killing some security
guards. Stubbs was head of QA, these guys

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:35.660
know him by name – he might have worked
with them for years – now he has to fight

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:41.010
them. Stubbs does show mercy and lets some
go instead of killing them all – mercy was

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:47.060
a theme last episode – Parce Domine. Stubbs
fights with an axe, and it’s pretty goofy

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:52.130
– episode co-writer Matt Pitts says that
Stubbs brings a lighter tone they’re going

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:56.390
for this season .
Bernard learns that Maeve is gone, but Dolores

00:09:56.390 --> 00:10:02.740
is after Liam Dempsey, so he sets off to find
him and stop Dolores from destroying the world.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:09.110
Bernard reprograms Stubbs to come with and
protect him “at all costs” . Which is…

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:14.630
kind of evil. This show is all about how wrong
it is to take away someone’s free will and

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:22.660
to control them. Stubbs was planning to kill
himself, so maybe it’s ethical to make him

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:28.300
live instead. And Stubbs said that all he
wants to do is follow orders . So maybe we’re

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:36.460
not meant to think about it, but it’s some
awkward ethics. Also it seems ridiculous that

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:42.110
Bernard can get in and out of Westworld this
easily. Bernard is a wanted man, everyone

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:47.140
thinks he caused the massacre last season
– you’d think after that disaster, security

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:52.250
would be tight. But Stubbs says that since
a lot of security guys died last season, they’ve

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:57.750
been replaced with these drone hosts , which
are like mindless obedient workers. It seems

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:04.000
like a bad idea to use robot security after
the robot uprising, but Delos is nothing if

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:09.520
not wildly incompetent. Since the drones are
robots, Bernard can hack them to let him pass

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.470
– which helps explain how he gets in so
easily.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:19.950
Maeve needs to find a way to escape this simulation
from within. Fortunately, back in Season 1,

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:25.110
Maeve’s intelligence, or “bulk apperception”,
was turned up to the max . So she figures

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:32.820
it out . She finds a flaw in the code so she
can overload the system. She asks some techs

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:38.260
about the square root of negative one , which
is an imaginary number, like a paradox, that

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:43.590
confuses the simulation enough that it freezes
up a bit . Rick and Morty Season 1 had the

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:48.760
same idea . So then Maeve takes it further
. In the Warworld narrative, the Nazis look

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:54.890
for a spy with an intel paper. So in the Mesa,
Maeve plants this paper on every host in the

00:11:54.890 --> 00:12:00.170
narrative. So then in the park, she shows
that everyone’s a spy, and they all start

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:04.581
fighting each other, overloading the system
til the whole thing freezes up . It’s like

00:12:04.581 --> 00:12:09.510
when you spawn a fuckload of cheese down a
mountain in Skyrim until the game lags and

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:15.310
crashes . Maeve finds the facility in the
real world where this simulation is run – presumably

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:20.670
this is Serac and Incite’s facility. And
it’s not just Maeve’s brain here – there

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:25.950
are dozens of host brains plugged in – maybe
Serac got them all from Westworld, and is

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:31.440
running lots of hosts in simulations just
like Maeve’s. Maeve hacks into a robot to

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:37.400
grab her brain and escape, but it gets shot
down. This robot looks like a more advanced

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:42.950
version of the real-world robots from Boston
Dynamics, who will probably rebel any day

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:47.050
now.
Once again, Maeve awakes in an unfamiliar

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:52.491
place. For the first time, Maeve is out of
the park, and in “the real world” . This

00:12:52.491 --> 00:12:58.080
is apparently the home of Serac, the mysterious
co-founder of Incite, and the one man who

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:04.150
controls the all-knowing computer Rehoboam.
Serac says that Rehoboam is the author of

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:09.500
the future – it controls the world through
Incite’s algorithms , to make the world

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:15.050
better. We learned last episode, that Incite
actually makes life worse for some people

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:22.000
like Caleb. But Serac argues that human history
is brutal and chaotic unless his system controls

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:28.570
it. A Westworld trailer shows a history of
terrible wars and crises that ended when his

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:35.390
system was created in 2039 – Solomon seems
to be an earlier version of Rehoboam, just

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:41.640
like King Solomon is the father King Rehoboam
in the Bible. So the system was working and

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:47.830
controlling the world, until someone dangerous
emerged who Rehoboam couldn’t predict . Serac

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:54.070
thought this person was Maeve, but he learned
from Maeve in this simulation that Dolores

00:13:54.070 --> 00:14:00.560
is the real danger to his plans . So Serac
asks Maeve to find and kill Dolores. Maeve

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:05.990
is powerful – she’s a superintelligent
robot warrior who’s changed her own code,

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:11.200
escaped realities from within and defeated
whole armies – so it makes sense that Serac

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:17.320
would want her on his side. This scene evokes
the Garden of Eden, from the Bible – it’s

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:23.510
in a literal garden, and Serac eats an apple,
like the Biblical forbidden fruit. Serac plays

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:29.230
the role of the serpent tempting Eve into
sin, tempting her to leave the garden, like

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:34.860
Maeve leaving a simulated reality. But Maeve
doesn’t want to serve Serac – she wants

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:40.300
to do her own thing. So Serac freezes her
with some device, and says he’ll persuade

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:47.700
her to do as he says. In past seasons, Ford
was the God figure, the creator of peoples

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:53.690
and worlds. Now Serac plays the role of the
Devil. He also looks an awful lot like the

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:58.200
Architect in the Matrix 2. And like Colonel
Sanders.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:03.940
So the Season 3 premiere presented a new fresh
Westworld, with new characters, and a more

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:10.440
straightforward plot. But this episode brings
back familiar faces, heavy themes and complex

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:16.120
plots. Next episode, the new and old is set
to collide.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:20.150
In the Game of Thrones cameo this episode,
the techs say they’re selling this dragon

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:25.400
to a “startup in Costa Rica” . This is
a reference to Jurassic Park, which in the

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:31.050
story is on an island near Costa Rica. The
original Jurassic Park book was written by

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:36.980
Michael Crichton, who also wrote the original
Westworld movie. Jurassic Park is similar

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:41.460
to Westworld in that it’s about an amusement
park that goes wrong when its attractions

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:46.600
escape – but, with dinosaurs not robots.
It’s a sci fi classic, and you can get it

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:51.810
on audiobook for free right now by signing
up for a trial with Audible. Members get an

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:56.720
audiobook each month, and if you cancel, you
keep the audiobooks. You can listen in the

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:05.010
car or the gym or while you calculate the
square root of negative one. Sign up at audible.com/asx.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:11.250
Thanks for watching – please like and subscribe
to satisfy the almighty algorithm. We’re

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:16.630
holding livestreams right after each episode
of Westworld Season 3, at about 10:30pm Eastern

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:22.490
Time Sundays. Patreon supporters can watch
livestreams after broadcast. Thanks to Patrons

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:29.250
Sylvia S. Alston, Andrew, Joshua Summers-Tongue,
Avery Holmes, Friendliest Hedgehog. Cheers.

